{
  "dom_id": "question-182684",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Suppose we wish to prove the following statement using mathematical induction:\n\n$4\\,∣\\,{5}^{n}-1$ for all $n\\in N$\n\nA proof template is outlined below. Fill in the missing statements.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=1.$\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}={{field-2}},\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-3}}\n$$\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=$ {{field-4}}, we have that\n\n$$\n{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{{field-6}}.\n$$\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, $4\\,∣\\,{5}^{n}-1$ for all $n\\in N.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
